作者: 烈火(fire)
题目: About changing the LPC engine.
日期: Tue Nov 23 05:03:23 1999
About Stefan's suggestion of changing LPC engine. I think we can consider
it. But not hurry, we will use some time to search the information of PIKE
and evaluate its potentiality and when we got familar with it and find it
is really a stable base, then we need to estimate the difficulty of migration.
and then do the migration.
  But the most important thing now is to finish this release first.
Because we have 
spent a lot time and energy on it. We simply need some results.
Somehow, perhaps
we can't put in every thing in the first release, but at least it works well
with the current stuff. It is obviously that we have some bugs in
the low level.
I hope we can figure them out and fix them. 
  Anyway, i think the mudos, even has some limitation, it is good
enough to support
current SanGuo Mud. and some of the shortage can be overcoverd.
Forexample, Mudos doesn't support access to database. It is sure now
we are using
some database based system. But unlike most database, the mapping
has it advantage
and also the number of records is not too big yet (no more than
2000). so perhaps
later we can invite some way to implenment some database operation
on small-sized
tables.
  About the Web, it is one part of the mud but not the essential
part for playing.
and we may use other web server and combined with our mud Cgi.
  Of course, if PIKE is far more advantaged than MudOS, we may shift
to it in the 
future, my opinion is that MudOS is capable to host this mud in
current stage :)
Regards
fire


